Description: live session of Legion started from a USB stick
 Prepares the live session when the kernel command line has legion.live,
 which only the live entries of the boot menu of a Legion image add. It
 creates the account "live" without a password, gives it administrator
 rights without a password prompt and logs it in automatically. The session
 stays light: no update checks or downloads and no software center service
 in the background.
 .
 Everything the session changes is in RAM, so nothing reaches the USB stick.
 On other starts this package does nothing. The Legion installer removes it
 from the installed system.

